27 0 obj
<</Parent 36 0 R/Next 28 0 R/Prev 26 0 R/Title(I. That we have a tremendous, ever swelling crowd of wage-earners which it is our business to house decently.)/Dest 872 0 R>>
endobj
28 0 obj
<</Parent 36 0 R/Next 29 0 R/Prev 27 0 R/Title(II. That it is not housed decently.)/Dest 873 0 R>>
endobj
29 0 obj
<</Parent 36 0 R/Next 30 0 R/Prev 28 0 R/Title(III. That it must be so housed here for the present, and for a long time to come, all schemes of suburban relief being as yet utopian, impracticable.)/Dest 874 0 R>>
endobj
30 0 obj
<</Parent 36 0 R/Next 31 0 R/Prev 29 0 R/Title(IV. That it pays high enough rents to entitle it to be so housed, as a right.)/Dest 875 0 R>>
endobj
31 0 obj
<</Parent 36 0 R/Next 32 0 R/Prev 30 0 R/Title(VI. That the security of the one no less than of the other half demands, on sanitary, moral, and economic grounds, that it be decently housed.)/Dest 876 0 R>>
endobj
32 0 obj
<</Parent 36 0 R/Next 33 0 R/Prev 31 0 R/Title(VII. That it will pay to do it. As an investment, I mean, and in hard cash. This I shall immediately proceed to prove.)/Dest 877 0 R>>
endobj
